      "side": 1,
      "message": "I try to follow how `clang-format` formats it (my editor is set to format with `clang-format`). Code that is in `platform2` has better support for `clang-format`, since the `platform2` uses the Google C++ style guide, which is better defined than the Linux kernel style guide used by EC.\n\nThe C++ style guide just [says to be consistent](https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Boolean_Expressions). I usually put them at the end:\n\n```\n\treturn match_result \u003d\u003d EC_MKBP_FP_ERR_MATCH_YES ||\n\t       match_result \u003d\u003d EC_MKBP_FP_ERR_MATCH_YES_UPDATED ||\n\t       match_result \u003d\u003d EC_MKBP_FP_ERR_MATCH_YES_UPDATE_FAILED;\n```",
